        ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{3 \\log{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\log{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x^{4}}\\cdot 4 x^{3}=\\frac{4}{x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\frac{1}{4}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3 \\log{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\log{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int u\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{u^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3 u^{2}}{8}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3 \\log{\\left(x^{4} \\right)}^{2}}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
